    "id": "p31-q59-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "59",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.\n$$\\frac{x^2-9x+20}{x^2-5x+4}\\times\\frac{x^2-3x+2}{x^2-5x+6}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{x-5}{x-3}$, $x\\ne1,2,3,4$.\n\nFactorise all four quadratics before cancelling.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2-9x+20}{x^2-5x+4}\\times\\frac{x^2-3x+2}{x^2-5x+6}&=\\frac{(x-5)(x-4)}{(x-1)(x-4)}\\times\\frac{(x-1)(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-3)}\\\\\\frac{x^2-9x+20}{x^2-5x+4}\\times\\frac{x^2-3x+2}{x^2-5x+6}&=\\frac{x-5}{x-3}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne1,2,3,4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
